{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.moravian.edu/career-success": {
      "title": "Laurie Riley ’82 Center for Career Success",
      "description": "Career Success | Moravian University Skip to main content Moravian Home Visit Apply Give Lighting the Way Info For Current Students Alumni Families Faculty & Staff Media Veterans Menu Search About Leadership Facts, Figures & Rankings History & Traditions Community Standards Campus Maps Mission Bethlehem, PA Partnerships News & Events Contact Academics Programs Elevate Experience Academic Support Research Study Abroad Academic Calendar Registrar's Office Reeves Library AMOS Institute for Moravian History & World Heritage School of Theology Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Associates Professional Studies Adult Undergraduate Visit Affordability Cost & Aid Request Information Apply Accepted First-Year Students Life Wellness Dining & Meal Plans Housing Career Success Events Calendar Book Shop Outcomes Internships & Externships Alumni Fellowship Program Moravian Magazine Giving Athletics Quick Actions Moravian Home Visit Apply Give Lighting the Way Info For Information For Current Students Alumni Families Faculty & Staff Media Veterans Moravian College Twitter Moravian College Facebook Moravian College Instagram Moravian University Youtube Moravian College LinkedIn Moravian College Tik Tok © 2026  Moravian University Search Search Keywords Search: Search Menu Career Success Students Alumni Employers Faculty and Staff About Us FAQs Outcomes Breadcrumb Moravian University Career Success Laurie Riley ’82 Center for Career Success Career Success Starts Here! Listed #17 in Best Career Services, Princeton Review: 2027 Edition At Moravian University’s Laurie Riley ’82 Center for Career Success, we’re dedicated to helping students and alumni turn their ambitions into achievements. Whether you're exploring majors, preparing for interviews, or launching your job search, our team is here to guide you every step of the way. From résumé and cover letter support to networking strategies and graduate school exploration, we provide the tools and connections to help you build a meaningful career. And it doesn’t stop there—our resources extend to employer partners looking to connect with top talent, as well as to faculty and staff eager to support student success. No matter where you are in your journey, we’re here to guide you forward with confidence. Schedule Your Appointment Laurie Riley ’82 Center for Career Success Receives National Excellence Award from NACE Moravian University's Laurie Riley ’82 Center for Career Success has been named the 2026 recipient of the Career Readiness Excellence Award from the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE). This prestigious award recognizes Moravian's best practices in career services that intentionally integrate career readiness competencies into work with students and alumni, strengthening preparation for internships and post-graduate careers. Opportunities and Resources At the Riley Center for Career Success, we’re all about opening doors and creating possibilities. Whether you're launching your career, growing your network, or looking for top talent, we provide the connections and support to help you succeed now and in the future! Students As a student, you'll collaborate with members of your career success team to explore career options, discuss internships, kickstart your job search, and much more. See Our Student Resources Career Success Team Career Readiness Badges Job and Internship Search Internships and Externships Career Resources Student Employment Program Alumni As valued members of the Moravian University community, our alumni can access a range of opportunities to stay connected, give back, and continue their professional growth. See Our Alumni Resources Available Career Services for Alumni Ways to Engage as Alumni Faculty and Staff Learn helpful tips to advise your students, enrich your classes with career-focused workshops, or collaborate with us on events and employer outreach. See Our Faculty and Staff Resources Career-Related Workshops Career and Major Exploration Competencies and Career Readiness Moravian Career Fairs, Events, and Employer Engagement Networking Tips Job and Internship Search Resources Faculty Advisory Board for Career Success Employers and Community Partners Explore diverse recruiting options to connect with top talent at Moravian University, or volunteer to ensure our programming aligns with current employer trends and needs. See Our Employer and Community Resources Recruiting Resources Employer Advisory Board Elevate Your Future Toward Career Success Working with the Riley Center for Career Success is a cornerstone of the Elevate experience—and a key to your future success. Through collaboration with your dedicated career success team and active participation in career success events, you’ll gain hands-on career exploration and support designed to prepare you for a meaningful, long-term career. Your Elevate journey can begin even before you arrive on campus. Starting the summer before your first year, you’ll have access to our Career Readiness Digital Badging platform , powered by Suitable . Throughout your undergraduate experience, you can earn points toward your digital badges by participating in a wide range of co-curricular and experiential learning activities—from attending campus events to completing internships. By completing your digital badges, you'll build a portfolio of real-world experiences and transferable skills that are highly valued by employers and graduate schools—and be one step closer to completing your Elevate experience, receiving cords to wear at graduation as a symbol of your achievement. In addition, if you complete all eight badges before graduation, complete an Elevate Travel experience or the RISE Teamwork & Leadership program, meet with a member of your career success team on a semesterly basis throughout your undergraduate career or a minimum of eight times total, and meet the 3.0 GPA expectation, you'll be eligible for the Elevate Career Promise . Click here for the full cost of attendance . Moravian College Twitter Moravian College Facebook Moravian College Instagram Moravian University Youtube Moravian College LinkedIn Moravian College Tik Tok 1200 Main Street Bethlehem, PA 18018 1 800.441.3191 610.861.1320 FAX: 610.625.7930 Make a Gift Information for Current Students Alumni Families Faculty & Staff Media Veterans Quick links Academic Calendar AMOS Book Shop Canvas School of Theology Reeves Library Contact Financial Aid Human Resources IT Directory Privacy Policy Disability Accommodation Appeal Non-Discrimination Title IX Community Standards Moravian University is committed to making its website accessible to all users. Should you find content that is inaccessible, please contact webaccessibility@moravian.edu or visit the Office of Disability and Accommodations ."
    },
    "https://www.moravian.edu/career-success/students/internships-externships": {
      "title": "Internships and Externships",
      "description": "Internships and Externships | Moravian University Skip to main content Moravian Home Visit Apply Give Lighting the Way Info For Current Students Alumni Families Faculty & Staff Media Veterans Menu Search About Leadership Facts, Figures & Rankings History & Traditions Community Standards Campus Maps Mission Bethlehem, PA Partnerships News & Events Contact Academics Programs Elevate Experience Academic Support Research Study Abroad Academic Calendar Registrar's Office Reeves Library AMOS Institute for Moravian History & World Heritage School of Theology Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Associates Professional Studies Adult Undergraduate Visit Affordability Cost & Aid Request Information Apply Accepted First-Year Students Life Wellness Dining & Meal Plans Housing Career Success Events Calendar Book Shop Outcomes Internships & Externships Alumni Fellowship Program Moravian Magazine Giving Athletics Quick Actions Moravian Home Visit Apply Give Lighting the Way Info For Information For Current Students Alumni Families Faculty & Staff Media Veterans Moravian College Twitter Moravian College Facebook Moravian College Instagram Moravian University Youtube Moravian College LinkedIn Moravian College Tik Tok © 2026  Moravian University Search Search Keywords Search: Search Menu Career Success Students Career Success Team Career Readiness Badges Job and Internship Search Internships and Externships Career Resources Student Employment Program Financial Literacy Alumni Employers Faculty and Staff About Us FAQs Outcomes Breadcrumb Moravian University Career Success Students Internships and Externships Internships and Externships What Is an Internship? An internship is a carefully monitored work experience in which an individual has intentional learning goals and reflects actively on what they’re learning throughout the experience. It’s temporary work that provides on-the-job training and practical experience. Internships usually last one semester but can be longer or shorter. Some are paid positions, and others can earn academic credit. Students can intern in almost any area of study in any part of the country or abroad. Internships often help students get their foot in the door for their first full-time permanent position. Employers use internships as a way to gain a first look at prospective employees. Explore where some of our students have interned! Logan Palau ’25 Podcast Production at iHeartMedia Ashley Rodrigues ’25 Digital Media at Living Sport for Super Bowl LIX Talia Collina ’25 Social Media at Cellar Beast Winehouse Dylan Fosko ’26 Tax intern at PwC & three more internships How to Complete an Internship for Credit Moravian University students may have the opportunity to earn academic credit for an internship beginning in their sophomore year. To be eligible, students must have a minimum 2.5 GPA. Transfer students must also have completed at least one full fall or spring semester at Moravian University. Exceptions may be considered with appropriate approval. Internships for credit combine hands-on professional experience with academic learning and reflection. Students completing an internship for credit work with both a faculty internship supervisor at Moravian and an on-site supervisor at the internship organization. Internships may be completed during the fall, spring, or summer and may be full-time or part-time. Students must complete the required number of internship hours based on the amount of academic credit they are seeking: 2 credits: Minimum of 70 internship hours 4 credits: Minimum of 140 internship hours 8 credits: Minimum of 280 internship hours Interested in Completing an Internship for Credit? Before registering, students should review the Internship for Credit information in AMOS , which includes eligibility requirements, the application and registration process, required forms, internship expectations, and important deadlines. Students are also encouraged to connect with their academic advisor and the Laurie Riley '82 Center for Career Success as they explore internship opportunities and determine whether completing an internship for credit is right for them. Current students: Visit AMOS → Internship for Credit, for complete instructions and next steps. Internship Stipends Internships often come with real-world hours, but not always real-world compensation. Internship stipends can help with that. Sponsored by local corporate partners and Moravian University alumni, these $2,500 (pretax) stipends provide financial support to selected students completing an internship for academic credit at Moravian University . Internship stipends are only available to students who are registered for an internship for academic credit during the semester in which the stipend is awarded. Applications for internship stipends open at the beginning of each academic semester, typically during the add/drop period . Eligible students completing an internship for credit that semester are encouraged to watch for application information and deadlines at the start of the term. Please Note: Internship stipend funding is limited, and the number of stipends available varies based on funding. Typically, 2–3 stipends are awarded each semester . Applications are reviewed by a committee, and awards are based on the strength of the application materials submitted. While all eligible students are encouraged to apply, funding is not guaranteed. Internship Stipend Application Form What Is an Externship? Externships provide Moravian University students the opportunity to connect with a professional in their area of interest. Through an externship, the student is able to experience an organization firsthand through short-term job shadowing and employer site visits. The goal of an externship is to help the student make educated career decisions when selecting an industry for their future employment. Externships typically take place during winter break. Students can register for an externship and review the available sites in the fall semester. Purpose of the Career Connections Externship Program The Career Connections Externship Program exists to provide Moravian University students the opportunity to connect with a professional in their area of interest. This program is designed to help students make educated career decisions relating to majors, job functions, and industries. The Career Connections Externship Program also gives students the opportunity to experience an organization firsthand, allowing them to make educated decisions when later selecting an industry for future employment. Benefits for students: Helps students with the school-to-work transition Builds a student’s professional network Better prepares students for the workplace by providing realistic information on occupations, skills, and responsibilities Better prepares students for next steps, such as internships and full-time positions Provides an increased understanding of employment trends and potential advancement in a specified field Provides exposure to a variety of departments and organizations that aid in selecting a future career path Benefits for the host/advisor: Provides an avenue to promote your chosen career to motivated and enthusiastic learners, and increase the visibility of your career and the benefits it offers Allows you to develop an advising relationship with a Moravian student while “giving back” to the university Increases your organization’s visibility on Moravian’s campus, as this program is aggressively marketed to students Helps you meet better-prepared and better-educated candidates Click here for the full cost of attendance . Moravian College Twitter Moravian College Facebook Moravian College Instagram Moravian University Youtube Moravian College LinkedIn Moravian College Tik Tok 1200 Main Street Bethlehem, PA 18018 1 800.441.3191 610.861.1320 FAX: 610.625.7930 Make a Gift Information for Current Students Alumni Families Faculty & Staff Media Veterans Quick links Academic Calendar AMOS Book Shop Canvas School of Theology Reeves Library Contact Financial Aid Human Resources IT Directory Privacy Policy Disability Accommodation Appeal Non-Discrimination Title IX Community Standards Moravian University is committed to making its website accessible to all users. Should you find content that is inaccessible, please contact webaccessibility@moravian.edu or visit the Office of Disability and Accommodations ."
